    {
      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50234861",
      "title": "LimonOS new OS no Unix no Linux",
      "source": "hackernews",
      "sourceName": "Hacker News",
      "summary": "Wrote everything myself from scratch in pure C without any Linux or pre-built distros. It&#x27;s a custom monolithic architecture with the Limine bootloader, custom drivers, window manager, and terminal.<p>As for models and agents: I used LLM agents as co-authors for routine tasks, writing tests, and debugging low-level code. I tuned them to strictly generate code without the standard library (libc) and to create host-side unit tests to verify modules before packing them into the kernel.<p>https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;AnonimusShamshiAlex&#x2F;LimonOS",
